          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": "Wait \u2014 the first `env.get_template('main.html')` after remove_alias didn't raise. Because Environment caches templates? No \u2014 Environment doesn't cache by default; `env.get_template` uses `self.cache`\u2026 actually, jinja2 Environment caches compiled templates in `self.cache` (LRUCache, default size 400). The first get_template('main.html') cached it, and remove_alias doesn't invalidate the cache. That's fine/expected behavior \u2014 a new Environment would raise. In my test, 'main.html' was already cached. The behavior is correct.\n\nBoth work. Done.\n\nBoth tasks are implemented in `src/jinja2/loaders.py`:\n\n**Task 1 (path_transform):** All loaders (`FileSystemLoader`, `PackageLoader`, `DictLoader`, `FunctionLoader`, `PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader`, `ModuleLoader`) accept an optional `path_transform` callable, applied before resolution; `BaseLoader.apply_path_transform` stores/applies it, and `None`/omission disables it. Transformed-not-found raises `TemplateNotFound` with the untransformed name.\n\n**Task 2 (aliases):** `BaseLoader` gains `add_alias`/`remove_alias`/`resolve_alias` (single-level, no chaining, safe remove, overwritable), resolved at the top of every `get_source`/`load`; a broken alias raises `TemplateNotFound` with the target name.\n\nAll 841 existing tests pass, and a sanity check confirms both features work end-to-end.",
